  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c **** /**
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  * @brief  Initialization function for the Q31 PID Control.
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  * @param[in,out] *S points to an instance of the Q31 PID structure.
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  * @param[in]     resetStateFlag  flag to reset the state. 0 = no change in state 1 = reset the sta
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  * @return none.
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  * \par Description:
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  * \par
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  * The <code>resetStateFlag</code> specifies whether to set state to zero or not. \n
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  * The function computes the structure fields: <code>A0</code>, <code>A1</code> <code>A2</code>
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  * using the proportional gain( \c Kp), integral gain( \c Ki) and derivative gain( \c Kd)
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  * also sets the state variables to all zeros.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/ControllerFunctions/arm_pid_init_q31.c ****  */
